  "en": {
    "kind": "Song cycle",
    "about": [
      "Theodorakis wrote the cycle in Paris in 1971–73 on eighteen poems by Yannis Ritsos (sixteen of them written on Leros in 1968, the last two on May Day 1970). It was first performed at the Albert Hall on 17 January 1973 with Maria Farantouri, Petros Pandis, Aphrodite Manou and Achilleas Kostoulis; the Paris recording was released in 1973 by EMI France.",
      "The Greek version, with Giorgos Dalaras and Anna Vissi on second voice, was recorded secretly in Greece under the junta and released by Minos in August 1974, after the dictatorship fell. It is the best-known form of the work."
    ]
